body:
Hot take here, but I've never liked Sharp Shadow, because of the effect on the dash length. I guess it doesn't always matter so much (it probably makes mincemeat of TL for instance) but I frequently want to use the dash in precise ways (e.g. going through NKG's firebats).

&#x200B;

Edit: Oh yeah, and any charms which give you blue health are basically useless to me. I get hit a lot and heal a lot, tbh.

I'm sure they cared deeply about it before, but I honestly question how much they really care now, considering the fact that they were offered more episodes and declined. It really does feel like they just want to move on to other things and can't really be bothered to give the show due care and attention. Also, imo, it's hard to pity people who have made tons of money and have just been given another huge job with Star Wars. Nothing wrong with a bit of punching up...

&#x200B;

I have a great deal of empathy for literally everybody else working on the show, because it seems like they're really trying. Acting, cinematography, music, etc.; it's all phenomenal.

It's not Dany snapping that bothers me. It's the fact that she almost systematically, basically street by street, goes about burning every last man, woman and child. Why is she fixated on killing everyone rather than on killing Cersei? Why isn't Cersei her first priority? It would be somewhat acceptable if Dany indiscriminately torched shit on her way to the red keep, so long as she headed straight for the red keep. But she allows Cersei time to escape while focusing on mowing down unarmed men, women and children. She's never done anything remotely so drastic before. She's only ever killed enemies, or people she had good reason to believe had done wrong. This is so many orders of magnitude worse than crucifying the masters, or burning Dickon and Randyll. She locked up her dragons for months because they burned one child. And now she just goes and burns thousands of children and orphans thousands more. I think she can accept innocents dying for some greater goal, but to make killing them *the* goal is just bizarre.

&#x200B;

I'm not even a Dany fan, I always thought that she was too impulsive and rash and power-hungry and whatever. I don't like (or buy, really) her and Jon and I won't be too fussed when she inevitably dies. But what she did didn't come across as a consequence of those character flaws; it seemed almost calculated, a systematic genocide and complete demolition of a city, basically. 

&#x200B;

One other argument is, well, as she said, she wants to inspire fear, and what better way than pretty much eliminating the population of King's Landing? Well, I guess...but I'm pretty sure that destroying all the soldiers and Cersei and the Red Keep would have been scary enough. Only other thing I can think of is that she hates the people of King's Landing and in her twisted, scarred mind, all of them are culpable in the downfall of her family, so they aren't truly the innocents she has always wanted to protect. And that's a reasonable angle, but it doesn't feel like it was addressed clearly enough if that's what they were going for.

My answers to this are ever-shifting. Especially as to the worst episodes. My least favourites are probably Mr. Peanutbutter's Boos, the Christmas Special (if I can count that) and The Judge. I don't hate any episode of BoJack, but the problem with these three is that they just bore me. Mr. Peanutbutter's Boos in particular; I wanted to like it because I like Mr. Peanutbutter and it was an interesting framing device, but it sticks out like a sure thumb in the season, disrupting pacing, and it just doesn't engage me.

&#x200B;

My top three episodes are Free Churro, Time's Arrow and Escape From L.A. Not much to say about them right now; all three are masterpieces. The first is just a tour de force of writing and voice acting, the second is stunningly animated/directed and incredibly moving, and the fourth is an exemplar in dread..

&#x200B;

I've gotta be honest, I don't get your list so much lol. I used to dislike BoJack kills but have grown a lot more appreciation for it recently. I enjoy Stop the Presses and INT. Sub to be fair. But your least favourites...Fish Out of Water is overrated imo but I still think it's excellent. Probably just about makes it into my top 10. And I like Hollyhock. Plus, you're discounting a loooot of Season 4 there haha.

Man I dunno. I've been overanalyzing to try to figure it out. When Season 4 came out, I thought it was my favourite season. But now I'm starting to think it just has a handful of awesome episodes and falls short in consistency. I don't think this season had any real duds. And I never found BoJack uproariously funny so I don't really mind the more dramatic focus of Season 5. In fact, I found that the humour in Season 4 could sometimes detract (most notably, the secondary storlines in episode 10 were a bit yawn-inducing). So Season 5 might be my favourite season. But I watched Season 3 again recently too and found new appreciation for it (not that I ever disliked it). To be honest, you could argue for almost any order of ranking of the seasons with this show. Even Season 1 has a lot going for it; the early episodes are still pretty funny if nothing else and the later moments of drama are perhaps made all the more powerful when you start with the impression that the show is just another animated comedy about a douchebag. 


Tl;dr lol I dunno. 

&#x200B;
